Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patch 0002.
Engram disk reads in spin mode, opt-in with VLLM_ENGRAM_DISK_SPIN_MS (ms the proxy keeps spinning after a lookup; 0 =
off, today's host node). In the k=3 profile the GPU idles a median 544 us a step on layer 1's Engram rows: 0002 reads
them in a CUDA host node that wakes a 256-thread pool on condition variables, three thread wake-ups per lookup on GB10
cores that take 0.1-0.4 ms each to wake, plus an NVMe that drops to a low-power state between decode steps. Spin mode:
enqueue_read puts three stream memory operations on the stream (request word = row count, wait for done = 1, reset),
captured into graphs like any node; one proxy thread per process spins on the request words, reads the rows with one
batch of native AIO O_DIRECT reads (io_uring is blocked by Docker's default seccomp profile) and sets done. While it
spins, a 4 KiB read every VLLM_ENGRAM_DISK_KEEPALIVE_US (default 2000, 0 = off) keeps the drive awake. Requests over
512 rows (prefill chunks) still go to the pread pool. Rows are bit-identical to 0002's (patches/engram_disk tests).
spark2, host side, 48 rows (96 reads) every 50 ms, cold: 0002's pool 1841 us p50; spin + AIO 667 us; + keep-alive 278.

